 "notes": "Paper presents updated CMB spectral distortion constraints on axion-photon coupling from COBE/FIRAS data. The coupling parameter \u03b5 in Eq. (3c) is defined as \u03b5 = [g_agamma * B_rms,T / (10^-10 GeV^-1 nG)]. Constraints depend critically on assumed primordial magnetic field strength B_rms \u2272 1 nG (Planck limit). Figure 11 shows FIRAS limits (solid line) as function of axion mass m_a. The paper treats both small distortion (perturbative) and large distortion regimes. Data points extracted from Fig. 11 FIRAS constraint curve (solid black line) by reading approximate values at decade intervals. Conversion from \u03b5 to g_agamma requires B_rms,T value; using B_rms,T \u2248 1 nG (near Planck limit) gives g_agamma \u2248 \u03b5 \u00d7 10^-10 GeV^-1. The constraint is mass-dependent due to frequency-dependent conversion redshifts. Multiple conversions occur for m_a \u2272 few \u00d7 10^-10 eV. Paper also discusses PIXIE forecasts (~2 orders of magnitude improvement). Confidence is moderate (0.75) because: (1) exact numerical values from Fig. 11 are approximate readings, (2) constraints depend sensitively on B-field assumption which is not uniquely specified in the paper, (3) coupling type is unambiguous but data extraction from plot introduces uncertainty. | vector-trace candidate: eps_limits_axion-new.pdf colour (1.0, 0.0, 0.0), 610 pts (selected among 12) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 610))",
